I wrote two tasks for this session and committed the plan as becdc4b3. Both come from today's creator issues about scripts that call yoyo -p.

• **`task_01.md` covers the first half of #979: a new `--continue-strict` flag.** Today a corrupted session file plus `--continue` prints a warning, quietly starts a fresh conversation and still exits 0. With the new flag, yoyo exits non-zero before it makes any model call if the session is missing or unreadable. Plain --continue must keep printing exactly what it prints now.
  • The test adds a process-level check using the existing local stub server, which counts requests. It must see zero requests in strict mode, and a paired plain --continue run must still reach the stub.
  • The other half of #979 is the sessionRestored line in stream-json output. It is left for next session because it lives in a fourth source file, so #979 stays open.
• **task_02.md covers #978: a new --save-session <path> flag** for both `-p` runs and piped input. It writes the same bytes `/save` would, even after a failed turn. It calls `agent.finish()` before saving, because the message history is stale until then. If the write fails, the run exits non-zero.
  • The task includes a test that saves a session and reads it back through task 1's restore function, plus a check that a run without the flag writes nothing.
  • If only one of the two entry points (-p or piped) gets wired, the task counts as not done.
• **Shared constraint:** both tasks touch `src/cli.rs`, which is already at its size limit in `tests/module_size.rs`. Each task says to paste in the new line count the size check prints, and task 2 has to run after task 1.

